1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,340
Last time, this room had a name.

2
00:00:02,790 --> 00:00:04,940
Today, it has something to say.

3
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:07,961
I flew the ship into the Vault,

4
00:00:08,411 --> 00:00:11,288
and a recording forty years old started to play.

5
00:00:13,088 --> 00:00:14,893
I didn't write a line of code for that.

6
00:00:15,793 --> 00:00:18,657
I wrote who's speaking, what he says,

7
00:00:19,107 --> 00:00:21,174
and how close the ship has to be.

8
00:00:22,374 --> 00:00:25,543
A place in a ruin can speak to two different listeners.

9
00:00:26,443 --> 00:00:28,897
One is the ship, which means the bridge,

10
00:00:29,347 --> 00:00:31,598
and that arrives on Comms as a call.

11
00:00:32,498 --> 00:00:34,127
The other is a person,

12
00:00:34,577 --> 00:00:37,981
a crew member who's gone outside in a suit and is standing there,

13
00:00:38,431 --> 00:00:40,484
and that's read on their handheld.

14
00:00:42,284 --> 00:00:44,349
The two are written differently.

15
00:00:45,249 --> 00:00:47,152
And here's the thing to know before we start:

16
00:00:47,602 --> 00:00:50,293
your crew doesn't leave the ship until a later lecture.

17
00:00:51,193 --> 00:00:54,079
So today you'll write both, and you'll play one.

18
00:00:54,529 --> 00:00:57,056
The other one, lint checks for you, and it waits.

19
00:00:58,256 --> 00:00:59,795
A call is placed by somebody,

20
00:01:00,245 --> 00:01:02,794
and a table of stone isn't a somebody.

21
00:01:03,694 --> 00:01:05,793
So I give the place a voice.

22
00:01:06,693 --> 00:01:09,723
Forty years ago a survey team found this ruin,

23
00:01:10,173 --> 00:01:12,362
and their leader left recordings in it.

24
00:01:14,162 --> 00:01:17,769
He's a character, written the way you wrote characters in Class 2,

25
00:01:18,219 --> 00:01:19,759
and his key is rook.

26
00:01:20,959 --> 00:01:23,229
Now the scene, and all of this is Class 2.

27
00:01:24,129 --> 00:01:25,983
The speaker is his key.

28
00:01:26,433 --> 00:01:29,111
When is hail, because this is a call that comes in.

29
00:01:30,011 --> 00:01:33,006
There's a title, which the crew reads before they open it.

30
00:01:33,906 --> 00:01:36,892
There are two takes, and the game picks one.

31
00:01:38,692 --> 00:01:40,601
Then come two answers.

32
00:01:41,051 --> 00:01:44,335
One leads on to a second scene, by its key,

33
00:01:44,785 --> 00:01:46,051
and one ends the call.

34
00:01:46,951 --> 00:01:49,987
The second scene has no When line and no title,

35
00:01:50,437 --> 00:01:53,206
because the only way into it is that answer.

36
00:01:54,406 --> 00:01:58,689
A scene is only words on a page, until something places the call.

37
00:01:59,589 --> 00:02:02,651
In Class 2 that was a beat, waiting to be revealed.

38
00:02:03,101 --> 00:02:05,265
This beat waits for the ship to get somewhere.

39
00:02:06,165 --> 00:02:10,228
It has three hashes, so it isn't a step of First Contact,

40
00:02:10,678 --> 00:02:13,467
and the word Beat is on its first line.

41
00:02:15,267 --> 00:02:17,029
Then comes the line that matters:

42
00:02:17,479 --> 00:02:21,119
starts when, reach altar, six hundred.

43
00:02:22,019 --> 00:02:23,283
Altar is a role.

44
00:02:23,733 --> 00:02:26,505
It's this word here, on the place's Roles line,

45
00:02:26,955 --> 00:02:29,225
and not its key or its name.

46
00:02:30,125 --> 00:02:32,452
For the Way In those differ:

47
00:02:32,902 --> 00:02:35,936
the key is way in, and the role is entrance.

48
00:02:37,736 --> 00:02:39,676
Six hundred is how close.

49
00:02:40,576 --> 00:02:42,653
The altar is in the middle of the Vault,

50
00:02:43,103 --> 00:02:44,896
and the wall is seven hundred out,

51
00:02:45,346 --> 00:02:48,449
so six hundred means the ship is in the room.

52
00:02:49,349 --> 00:02:50,522
Always write that number.

53
00:02:50,972 --> 00:02:53,642
Leave it out and the game uses five thousand,

54
00:02:54,092 --> 00:02:56,006
which is bigger than the whole ruin.

55
00:02:56,906 --> 00:02:59,855
Last comes Action, which says who calls,

56
00:03:00,305 --> 00:03:03,421
then the word hails, and then the scene.

57
00:03:04,621 --> 00:03:06,292
You know what an answer can do:

58
00:03:06,742 --> 00:03:09,991
it can start a quest, finish one, or send a word.

59
00:03:10,891 --> 00:03:12,722
In a ruin there's one more,

60
00:03:13,172 --> 00:03:16,317
which is reveal, and then a place.

61
00:03:17,217 --> 00:03:19,885
Remember the Niche, the place I hid last time.

62
00:03:20,336 --> 00:03:23,603
It only showed up when the ship was nearly on top of it.

63
00:03:24,503 --> 00:03:28,145
With this answer, it shows up when Comms says so.

64
00:03:29,945 --> 00:03:31,029
Now be careful here.

65
00:03:31,479 --> 00:03:35,630
Reveal takes the place's key, the word in round brackets,

66
00:03:36,080 --> 00:03:37,953
and reach took its role.

67
00:03:38,853 --> 00:03:42,356
That's two lines, and two different words for the same place.

68
00:03:43,556 --> 00:03:44,870
Now for the other listener.

69
00:03:45,770 --> 00:03:49,622
Somebody is standing at this table, and nobody's calling them.

70
00:03:50,072 --> 00:03:52,108
What they read is what they see.

71
00:03:53,008 --> 00:03:54,993
On the place I add two lines.

72
00:03:55,443 --> 00:03:57,151
Scene is the key of a scene,

73
00:03:57,601 --> 00:04:00,412
and Scan is one line about the place,

74
00:04:00,862 --> 00:04:03,964
for whoever comes after the scene has been played.

75
00:04:05,764 --> 00:04:07,673
The scene itself has no fence at all.

76
00:04:08,573 --> 00:04:11,053
There's no speaker, because nobody's speaking,

77
00:04:11,503 --> 00:04:14,771
and no title, because it isn't a call.

78
00:04:15,671 --> 00:04:17,070
One rule is new:

79
00:04:17,520 --> 00:04:22,235
every path through a place's scene has to end in an answer with empty brackets,

80
00:04:22,685 --> 00:04:24,323
because nothing else closes it.

81
00:04:26,123 --> 00:04:30,217
This opens when a crew member's suit arrives here, and not when the ship does.

82
00:04:31,117 --> 00:04:32,742
So I can't show it to you today,

83
00:04:33,192 --> 00:04:34,847
and you can't play it today.

84
00:04:35,747 --> 00:04:38,152
We come back to it when the crew can leave the ship.

85
00:04:39,352 --> 00:04:41,361
So I run lint, and it's clean.

86
00:04:42,261 --> 00:04:43,532
Now I break the role,

87
00:04:43,982 --> 00:04:48,097
and lint tells me that nothing in the mission wears a role called alter.

88
00:04:48,997 --> 00:04:52,064
That's good, because that call would never have come.

89
00:04:53,864 --> 00:04:56,329
Next I break the scene on the place.

90
00:04:56,779 --> 00:05:00,257
Lint tells me the Altar points at a scene that isn't there,

91
00:05:00,707 --> 00:05:03,536
and that's how I check the half I can't play.

92
00:05:05,336 --> 00:05:07,285
Now the word after reveal.

93
00:05:07,735 --> 00:05:10,501
Lint tells me nothing in the mission has that key,

94
00:05:10,951 --> 00:05:12,986
so the answer would do nothing.

95
00:05:13,886 --> 00:05:16,923
But if I put a room's key there, lint says clean,

96
00:05:17,373 --> 00:05:19,618
and the game would say nothing either.

97
00:05:20,068 --> 00:05:23,154
The answer would end the call, and the Niche would stay dark.

98
00:05:24,054 --> 00:05:27,168
So read two things yourself, every time:

99
00:05:27,618 --> 00:05:30,433
that the word after reveal is a place,

100
00:05:30,883 --> 00:05:33,302
and that there's a number after the role.

101
00:05:34,502 --> 00:05:37,392
In through the Mouth we go, and across the Nave.

102
00:05:38,292 --> 00:05:41,071
Up the tunnel, and there's the Altar on the map,

103
00:05:41,521 --> 00:05:42,858
the same as last time.

104
00:05:43,758 --> 00:05:45,276
Now into the room.

105
00:05:47,076 --> 00:05:48,820
And on Comms, there's a call:

106
00:05:49,270 --> 00:05:52,107
Surveyor Rook, a recording at the altar.

107
00:05:53,007 --> 00:05:56,189
I open it, and I get one of my two takes.

108
00:05:57,089 --> 00:05:59,707
I play the rest, and then I mark the Gallery.

109
00:06:01,507 --> 00:06:03,484
Back on Helm, there's the Niche,

110
00:06:03,934 --> 00:06:05,134
and we haven't been near it.

111
00:06:06,334 --> 00:06:07,336
Now it's your turn.

112
00:06:08,236 --> 00:06:12,372
Give the Niche a recording of its own, and words of its own.

113
00:06:13,272 --> 00:06:15,375
Make one answer finish a quest.

114
00:06:16,275 --> 00:06:18,694
Then break one line where lint can see it,

115
00:06:19,144 --> 00:06:20,519
and one where it can't.

116
00:06:22,319 --> 00:06:25,007
Next time, the crew learns something in one room,

117
00:06:25,457 --> 00:06:26,787
and uses it in another.
